reference[35]: "Local by default; --machine selects a configured SSH host. SSH admission,","classes, budget, owner room, state, deadlines and cleanup are remote-authoritative.",Remote jobs use the configured workdir and remote environment; stdin is /dev/null,(the SSH stdin channel is reserved for session liveness). Disconnect cancels the,remote process group and reclaims its lease. No worktree transfer or daemon.,"Reserve logical cores and memory minus owner room, FIFO","(no backfill). Defaults: --class default (1 core, up to 1GiB, timeout 1h),","--wait 30m. --cores, --memory and --timeout override class defaults.","Memory: integer bytes or KiB/MiB/GiB/KB/MB/GB. Durations: positive Go durations;","--wait 0 tries once. Oversized requests fail with 2 before starting a child.",BERTH_CONFIG selects strict JSON config; default ~/.config/berth/config.json,(or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/berth/config.json). Budget defaults derive from the host.,Jobs run in a process group owned by the berth job PID. Use noninteractive,commands; no terminal job-control,handoff is provided. Deadline,"or cancellation terminates the group (TERM, then KILL after 1s); sweep reclaims",after owner death or expiry. Children that call setsid can escape the group.,"Reservations are cooperative admission, not hard CPU/memory limits.","Child stdin/stdout/stderr pass through unchanged, including with --json;","--json applies only to pre-start errors. Post-start cleanup errors go to stderr","and retain the lease, never replacing the child's exit code.","Examples:","  berth job --cores 2 --memory 2GiB --timeout 10m -- go test ./...","  berth job --class suite --wait 0 -- make check","Output: --axi for agents, --json for scripts (mutually exclusive).","Default: human on terminals; AXI for pipes or BERTH_AXI=1.","Lease commands: --full restores complete AXI records/text; JSON is always complete.","","Exit codes: 0 success (including no-ops), 1 operation failed, 2 invalid usage.","berth job: child's exit code on completion; 124 deadline killed child;",75 (EX_TEMPFAIL) no slot within wait. Berth's own 1/2 apply only when no child,was started. Signal termination returns 128 + signal number. Helper/wait,failures after start use 125/126 and diagnostics on stderr.,76 is SSH transport/protocol failure with unknown remote result (stderr).,Child exit 255 is preserved and is not confused with SSH failure.
usage: "berth job [--machine NAME] [--cores N --memory M --class C --timeout D --wait W] -- <cmd...>"
